:''Not to be confused with [[Wave Attack]]s or [[Explosion]]s.''
'''Surge Attacks''' (烈波, ''Reppa'', '''Intense Waves'''), also known as just '''Surges''', are a [[Special Abilities|special ability/effect]] in [[The Battle Cats]]. They can be created by certain [[:Category:Surge Attack Cats|Cat Units]] and [[:Category:Surge Attack Enemies|Enemy Units]] at a set chance. This ability was added in [[Version 9.2 Update|Version 9.2]].
[[File:Uril surge.gif|thumb|right|[[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Mystic Uril]] creating a Surge Attack]]

==Explanation==
Surge Attacks share many qualities with [[Wave Attack]]s: they hit all enemies/cats in their range, but don't affect bases (excluding most [[:Category:Animated Enemy Bases|animated ones]]), and they deal the same damage as a normal attack from their creator; they will also retain any special ability/effect that the original attack had, except for [[Attacks Only]]. Unlike Wave Attacks, however, Surge Attacks '''stay in one spot''', dealing the original damage of the [[Cat Units|Cat]] or [[Enemy Units|Enemy]] unit to opposing units every 20f.

Surge Attacks have a '''level''', which, unlike a Wave Attack's level, determines how long they will linger on the field for. A level 1 Surge lasts for 20f, and each additional level increases the duration by 20f and allows the Surge to hit the same target one more time. Unlike Wave Attacks, Surge Attacks have a '''designated area''' where they can spawn, which varies depending on the unit. This value is independent from the attack range and will determine the minimum and maximum range in which the attack can appear.

Despite looking similar, Surges are '''entirely separate''' from Waves/Explosions; Immune to Waves/Explosions, Wave Shield and Resist Wave will not protect against Surges, and Immune to Surge and Resist Surge will not protect against Waves/Explosions. Notably, there is a 15-frame delay before the Surge spawns, and a 20 frame delay between each individual Surge hitbox. The frame delay correlates with each gained Surge level.

'''To recap:'''
#A Surge has a single spawn point, which is a single point within the area of effect.
#A Surge has 375 range width. Starting from spawn point, it has 125 outward piercing range and 250 inner range.
#Surges cannot harm bases, excluding most animated bases found within the [[Catclaw Dojo]] and elsewhere.
#Surge damage is the same as the damage of the hit that caused it (if a unit has Multi-Hit, the Surge bases its damage on only the hit associated with it, not the total attack power). Example: if a unit with 200 attack power deals 3 hits (each hit in order respectively: deals 100, 50, 50 damage; with the 1st and 2nd creating a Surge), the 1st Surge will deal 100 damage with every hit, the 2nd one deals 50 per hit.
#Every hit of a Surge carries all the exact effects from the hit (only its associated hit if there's Multi-Hit, applying the same principle for damage calculation) that caused it. If the initial hit lands a freeze despite a low probability, all hits of the Surge will always freeze; and if the initial hit doesn't, then none of the Surge's hits will freeze (meaning, every Surge hit doesn't reroll its chance, instead directly inheriting the success or failure of the initial hit).
#There is a 15f (0.5s) gap time between main attack and Surge spawning, and a 20f (0.67s) gap time between every hit of the Surge.

==Calculating Effective DPS of Surge Attackers==
DPS of a Surge unit can be calculated using the formula:
'''Surge DPS = Base DPS x Surge Level'''. Following this, a Level 30 Master Uril has a base DPS of 803 and a Surge Level of 3. So his Surge carries a DPS of 2409 if all hits connect. This also reflects onto the damage per hit a unit has.

For units who may hit foes with both the main attack and the Surge, simply add one to the Surge level to get the full DPS of the attack: '''Maximum DPS = Base DPS + Surge DPS = Base DPS x (Surge Level + 1)'''.

For example, a level 30 [[Kasli the Bane (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasli, Daughter of Chaos]] has a base DPS of 2,931 and a Surge Level of 3. So her Surge carries a DPS of 8,793 if all hits connect and, if her initial attack also hits the target, she has an effective DPS of 11,724.

Since Mini-Surges are nearly identical in every way besides damage, the formula for calculating the DPS for mini surge attackers is as follows:  '''Mini-Surge DPS = Base DPS x (Mini-Surge level / 5)'''. For units who hit with their main attack and mini-surge, calculate the full DPS of the attack using this formula: '''Maximum DPS = Base DPS + Mini-Surge DPS = Base DPS x (Mini-Surge Level / 5) + Base DPS'''

==Mini-Surge==
[[File:705 c attack animation.gif|thumb|right|[[King of Doom Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|King of Extinction Phono]] creating a Mini-Surge]]
'''Mini-Surge''' (小烈波 ''Shō Reppa'', '''Mini Intense Wave''') is an ability introduced in [[Version 12.3 Update|Version 12.3]]. Mini-Surges are almost identical to regular Surges, but are visually smaller and deal only 20% of their creator's attack power. Like how [[Wave Attack|Mini-Waves]] are considered the same effect as waves, Mini-Surges are still counted as Surges, meaning they are resisted by all the same abilities.

Since the added attack power from Attack Up [[Talent Orbs]] is a flat increase that ignores damage multipliers, it will be added on top of the Mini-Surge's damage without being decreased to 20%. Technically, this means units with multi-level Mini-Surges (e.g., [[Talents|Ultra Talented]] [[Coppermine (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Coppermine κ]]) can reap more benefit from Attack Up Talent Orbs than any other unit.

==Death Surge==
'''Death Surge''' (デス烈波 ''Desu Reppa'', '''Death Intense Wave''')  is an ability introduced in [[Version 10.9 Update|Version 10.9]] and exclusive to certain [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku Enemies]]. It is a post-mortem attack, which happens automatically with a short animation once an Aku with this ability dies. Visually, this is represented by a unique Aku soul instead of a regular white soul emerging. This unique-looking Aku soul activates the Surge Attack before disappearing. The Surge, unlike a regular Surge Attack, spawns directly every time, without the need of a regular attack connecting, plus, since it happens after death, it is not affected by any debuff that may have been applied to the dying enemy before their demise. In other words, there is no way to prevent the Surge from happening, nor can the Surge be made less problematic by ensuring that the enemy causing it dies with weaken or curse applied. [[File:Aftermath.gif|thumb|center|[[Condemned Peng|Condemned Peng]] creating a Death Surge]]

==Mini-Deathsurge==
'''Mini-Deathsurge''' (デス小烈波 ''Desu Shō Reppa'', '''Death Mini Intense Wave''')  is an ability introduced in [[Version 14.3 Update|Version 14.3]] and exclusive to Mini-Deathsurge [[Talent Orbs]]. With this Orb equipped, every second unit deployed has a 100% chance to create a Lv.1 Mini-Surge at 200~500 upon death, dealing 3-20% of its attack power as damage depending on the Orb's Rank. When two Mini-Deathsurge Orbs are equipped by the same unit, only one takes effect; the higher-Ranked Orb has priority. When a unit is set to create a Mini-Deathsurge, its deployment button will briefly flash and a small icon of the Orb will appear on the top-left corner of it.

