==Notes==
*Surge Attacks are only generated if their user's attack connects with an opposing unit or base.
*Surge Attacks operate at a delay, and they are a separate hitbox from the attack which triggered them, meaning that if the unit which created the surge is knocked back, the surge will still be on the battlefield and deal damage independently.
*Some abilities reduce the effect of Surge Attacks:
**[[:Category:Cats with Surge Immunity|Cats]] and [[:Category:Enemies with Surge Immunity|enemies]] with "Immune to Surge" abilities take no damage from Surge Attacks. However, they still can take damage from the attack triggering the Surge Attack if they are too close to the attacker.
**[[:Category:Resist Surge Cats|Cats with "Resist Surge" Talents]] or Resist Surge [[Talent Orbs]] take reduced damage from Surge Attacks. The damage reduction depends on the Talent's/Orb's level/Rank, generally ranging from 5% to 50% reduction. These effects stack, resulting in full immunity with either two S-Rank Resist Surge Orbs or one S-Rank Resist Surge Orb and a level 10 Resist Surge Talent.
*The [[Ototo Corps#Foundation and Style Upgrades|Waterblast Foundation]] reduces the damage all [[Cat Units]] take from Surge Attacks by 0.75% per level up to a maximum of 15%.
*Surge Attacks carry any [[Special Abilities|abilities]] that the original hit has. For example, [[Kasli the Bane (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasli the Bane]]'s surges curse all enemies.
*Surge Attacks are entirely separate from [[Wave Attack]]s and [[Explosion]]s.

